results/
# but keep the published HumanEval benchmark summaries (evidence for README claims)
!bedrock/benchmark/results/
!bedrock/benchmark/results/**/summary.json
!bedrock/benchmark/results/**/summary_rescored.json
!bedrock/benchmark/results/**/results_rescored.csv
docs-local/
FINDINGS.md
PLAN.md
REINVENT_SUBMISSION.md
MEDIUM_ARTICLE.md
ONE_PAGER.md
*.pem
*.key
*.log
# vLLM server / benchmark logs are tee'd to the console AND to this dir; never commit them
self-hosted/vllm/logs/
.env
.env.*
.scratchpad/

# Benchmark run output. This repository publishes NO run output: not the design
# artifacts, not the per-task metrics, not the judge scores, not the agent event
# streams. Only the directory's own README is tracked. The previous rules here
# ignored just the cloned target repos (<repo>/repo/), which left every artifact
# a run writes -- metrics.json, eval.json, patch.diff and multi-megabyte
# *-stream.jsonl -- committable by a plain `git add -A` after a benchmark, while
# three docs stated the opposite. Ignore the tree and re-include the README.
# (Upstream re-includes metrics.json, eval.json and run-summary.json so its runs
# are inspectable from git. That is the one place this rule deliberately differs:
# here those files are measured results, which this repository does not publish.)
benchmarks/swe-benchmark-data/**
!benchmarks/swe-benchmark-data/
!benchmarks/swe-benchmark-data/README.md

# Per-task target-repo clones. The harness clones into
# <clone_dir>/swe-clone-<task-id>/ (clone_dir defaults to /tmp, outside the
# repo) and deletes them after each task; this is the backstop for a config that
# points clone_dir inside the repo, so a leftover clone from a killed run can
# never be committed. The swe-clone- prefix is specific enough that this never
# matches the swe-benchmark-data output tree.
swe-clone-*/
**/swe-clone-*/

# Stray repo-root writes from a benchmark session: an agent handed a bare
# relative filename instead of the absolute artifacts_dir drops the file here,
# because both harnesses run the agent with cwd=REPO_ROOT. Named individually
# rather than by glob so an ordinary new doc at the root is not silently ignored.
/completion_confirmation.md
/task_completion_report.txt
/github-issue.md
__pycache__/
*.pyc
credentials.json
.aws/
secrets/
security-review-findings.xlsx
.litellm.pid
.mantle-token
# HuggingFace token for gated/faster model downloads — never commit; consumed by vllm-serve.sh
.hf_token
**/.hf_token
.DS_Store
.venv/
tmp/
.claude/worktrees/
# The runner config holds the endpoint and, unless api_key_env is used, a literal
# API key. Two docs and the onboard-benchmark skill tell every new user to create
# this file and state that it is gitignored; until now it was not.
benchmarks/config/runner.yaml

# HuggingFace token, second spelling (see .hf_token above).
.hftoken
**/.hftoken
